  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing the Root Causes of Irregular Migration Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to reduce irregular migration in Guatemala by connecting Guatemalans to opportunities to achieve prosperous, secure and dignified lives. It contributes to the government of the United States of America&apos;s regional Root Causes Strategy and is closely aligned with USAID Guatemala&#x2019;s 2020 &#x2013; 2025 Country Development Cooperative Strategy. The project likewise reflects IOM&#x2019;s commitments to protect migrants from the multiple dangers brought about by irregular cross-border movements and advance Sustainable Development Goal 10.7 to facilitate orderly, safe, and responsible migration. This project materializes in tailored research, targeted activities, mainstreaming approaches and sensitive programming.</narrative>
  </description>
